※ pl4g-test: compile=ok opt=0,1
※ pl4g-test: run=native,qemu exit=200
※ pl4g-test: diag=none

※ A variable of every width is written and read back, so that each store the
※ backends know is exercised on every architecture.
※
※ The values stay within what one instruction can carry on every target: the
※ tightest is the twelve-bit signed immediate of one of them, so a larger
※ constant would need a sequence this compiler does not generate yet.
let mut byte_value: u8 = 0u8
let mut half_value: u16 = 0u16
let mut word_value: u32 = 0u32
let mut wide_value: u64 = 0u64

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    byte_value ← 200u8
    half_value ← 1000u16
    word_value ← 2000u32
    wide_value ← 1500u64
    byte_value
